From bbdb5d1acb083c489b4e5cbe9c10c7b85b336305 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: P4R4D16M4 <patrickheinzelbecker@googlemail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 10:05:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 03/16] V585: vendor PFE driver (scpcom pfe_ctrl, pfe_13_00_2)
 as module

- import drivers/pfe_ctrl and drivers/pfe from scpcom/linux ls1024a-6.1.y
  (a8447d65), Kbuild paths fixed for O= builds, -Werror dropped
- pfe_platform: map the linked IRAM node (upstream mapped the PFE APB
  window as IRAM and the IPsec init wrote ARAM rings there); take the
  HIF IRQ from the DT resource instead of a GIC node-name lookup
- DT: pfe-iram and fsl,ls1024a-pfe-ctrl node (inert without PFE_CTRL)
- board: set system_rev from the C2K DEVICE_ID register (UTIL firmware
  selection, as the stock ATAG path did)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
